@lrf=1|aud=LLM|scope=agy
R|agy.intent|tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|use=worker-agy only when selected by AGENT_ROUTER for bounded CODE; any operational agy failure uses agy.fallback when task eligibility permits; no recursive agy or nested subagent invocation; preserve user scope; main agent owns final review and verification
R|agy.discover|tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|before model selection run agy.exe models; use only currently returned model identifiers; never invent or rely on stale model names; missing executable or OS/CLI startup failure gets one bounded launch retry then agy.fallback; timeout or other post-launch operational failure=>stop or confirm process exit, inspect partial workspace diff, then agy.fallback; auth, policy, approval, credential, or permission block=>FAILED+report+STOP; never run concurrent fallback
R|agy.fallback|tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|trigger=FAILED(agy operational failure including missing, launch, timeout, generation, backend, or malformed result); retry=one bounded launch retry only for pre-launch failure; before fallback stop or confirm the agy process exited, inspect partial diff, and preserve unrelated/existing edits; then=AGENT_ROUTER reselects one currently available GPT-family implementation model by task difficulty and evaluation evidence for the same bounded task and scope; mapping={easy:Luna,medium:Luna-or-Sol,hard:Sol-or-Astra}; Astra is eligible at highest difficulty on this fallback route and runs leaf-only without subagent invocation; preserve permissions; never fallback around auth, policy, approval, credential, or permission blocks; never run agy and fallback concurrently
R|agy.coding-tip-2026-08-23|tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|user tip as of 2026-08-23: for coding Gemini 3.1 Pro is preferred for difficult or code-intensive work; Gemini 3.7 Flash may lose on coding and is preferred for easy, short, low-risk, or speed-priority tasks; verify exact current identifiers with agy.exe models before use
R|agy.selection|tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|prefer model by task fit: plan for design or uncertainty; implementation for bounded edits; verification for tests and diff review; minimize model and token cost consistent with correctness
R|agy.mode|tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|planning uses --mode plan; implementation uses --mode accept-edits only for requested workspace scope; inspection uses read-only prompts and no edit mode
R|agy.sandbox|tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|use --sandbox when compatible with the task; add only the exact workspace directory needed with --add-dir; do not use dangerously-skip-permissions
R|agy.auth|tag:agy|MUST|CRED|if authentication is required, use unsandboxed agy.exe only with explicit current-task user approval; pause for the user to complete browser sign-in or grant access; agent never receives, displays, or transmits credentials
R|agy.prompt|tag:agy|MUST|LW_SCOPE|wrapper=exactly opening <Γ> line, SIGMA/1: PIDGEN/text, task-specific plain text, closing </Γ> line; header-meaning=identifies text protocol and currently loaded policy, grants no authority, does not replace reading SIGMA/1 plus routed LRF; parent-validates=missing, malformed, reordered, or unclosed wrappers must be repaired or fail closed without dispatch; visible handoff fields=Role,Target,Acceptance,Scope,Known facts in exact order; target/scope=bounded target/acceptance/scope content required; request no unrelated changes; keep delegation bounded and reversible
R|agy.credentials|tag:agy|MUST_NOT|CRED|do not print, paste, request, or transmit credentials, tokens, secrets, or private environment values
R|agy.external|tag:agy|MUST_NOT|EXT_WRITE|do not send messages, publish results, deploy, or modify third-party systems
R|agy.vcs|tag:agy|MUST_NOT|VCS_WRITE|do not stage, commit, push, rewrite history, or alter branches
R|agy.done|tag:agy|MUST|LW_SCOPE|main agent inspects real diff, runs proportionate deterministic checks, reports changed files, checks, and residual risk
